{"id":"A1-L074","title":"Adverbs of frequency: production and review","cefr":"A1","level":"A1","unit":"A1-U05","focus":"Adverbs of frequency — produção e revisão","targets":{"grammar":"Adverbs of frequency — produção e revisão","pron":"bed/bad","verbs":["understand"],"pv":[],"expr":["take a break"],"words":["accent","understand","break","should","arrive","ask","late","coffee"],"field":"Trabalho","genre":"Blog, diário, crônica","skill":"Escuta","words_min":8},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 74 · Adverbs of frequency: production and review","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Adverbs of frequency — produção e revisão.","**Verbos:** understand.","**Expressões:** take a break.","**Pronúncia:** bed/bad.","**8 palavras novas** (trabalho).","**Texto do dia:** blog, diário, crônica."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (A1):** eu consigo escrever um blog sobre minha rotina de trabalho com understand e take a break."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["Você ainda não faz as provas, mas já treina o formato de tarefas curtas que elas usam.","Esta aula treina **ouvir e anotar informações (IELTS Listening, TOEFL Listening)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["accent","sotaque"],["understand","entender"],["break","pausa"],["should","deveria"],["arrive","chegar"],["ask","perguntar"],["late","atrasado"],["coffee","café"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A blog post","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"A Day in My Office Life","paras":["I **always** arrive at nine. I **usually** work for two hours, then **take a break**. I **often** drink coffee, but I **never** eat at my desk.","I **sometimes** don’t **understand** my boss’s accent. I **rarely** say so. I should ask more often!"],"kicker":"WORK BLOG","by":"Ben","gloss":[["accent","sotaque"],["should","deveria"],["arrive","chegar"],["ask","perguntar"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Ben arrives at nine.","ans":"T","why":"“always arrive at nine.”"},{"q":"Ben eats at his desk.","ans":"F","why":"“never.”"},{"q":"Ben sometimes doesn’t understand his boss.","ans":"T","why":"“sometimes.”"}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“accent” means…","opts":["sotaque","acento gráfico","tom"],"ans":0,"why":"accent."},{"q":"“should” means…","opts":["deveria","pode","quer"],"ans":0,"why":"should."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Frequency: production","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Posição","Exemplo"],"rows":[["antes do verbo","**I always arrive early.**"],["depois de be","**She is never late.**"],["início/fim (sometimes, usually)","**Sometimes I work late. / I work late sometimes.**"]],"cap":"Frequency: production"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Com **do/does**: *Do you always…? I don’t often…*"}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"I ___ take a break at eleven. (usually)","a":"usually","why":"antes do verbo."},{"s":"She is ___ late. (never)","a":"never","why":"depois do be."},{"s":"I ___ understand the accent. (don’t always)","a":"don’t always","why":"negativa."},{"s":"Let’s take a ___ . (break)","a":"break","why":"take a break.","say":"take a break"}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["accent","sotaque"],["understand","entender"],["break","pausa"],["should","deveria"],["arrive","chegar"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["Coffee","Good","idea"],"ans":"Good idea Coffee","pt":"Boa ideia. Café?"},{"words":["break","Let's","take","a"],"ans":"Let's take a break","pt":"Vamos fazer uma pausa."}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"accent","pos":"word","pt":"sotaque","ex":"A strong accent.","expt":"Um sotaque forte."},{"w":"understand","pos":"word","pt":"entender","ex":"I understand you.","expt":"Entendo você."},{"w":"break","pos":"word","pt":"pausa","ex":"A short break.","expt":"Uma pausa curta."},{"w":"should","pos":"word","pt":"deveria","ex":"I should ask.","expt":"Eu deveria perguntar."},{"w":"arrive","pos":"word","pt":"chegar","ex":"Arrive on time.","expt":"Chegue na hora."},{"w":"ask","pos":"word","pt":"perguntar","ex":"Ask more.","expt":"Pergunte mais."},{"w":"late","pos":"word","pt":"atrasado","ex":"Never late.","expt":"Nunca atrasado."},{"w":"coffee","pos":"word","pt":"café","ex":"Some coffee.","expt":"Um pouco de café."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**take a break** — fazer uma pausa"]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"understand","pt":"entender","forms":[["I / you / we / they understand","I understand the lesson."],["he / she / it understands","She understands me."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Break time","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Break time","lines":[["Ben","Let’s take a break.","Vamos fazer uma pausa."],["Ana","Good idea. Coffee?","Boa ideia. Café?"],["Ben","Always! Do you understand the boss?","Sempre! Você entende o chefe?"],["Ana","Not always.","Nem sempre."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: bed/bad","items":[{"label":"bed/bad","note":"/ɛ/ (bed) × /æ/ (bad): abra mais a boca no /æ/.","words":["bed","bad","men","man","pen","pan"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Describe your work day with frequency adverbs.","pt":"Descreva.","model":"I always arrive at nine. I usually take a break."},{"q":"Say what you don’t understand.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I don’t always understand the accent."},{"q":"Suggest a break.","pt":"Sugira.","model":"Let’s take a break."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a 6-line blog about your day.","model":"I always arrive at nine. I usually work for two hours. Then I take a break. I often drink coffee. I never eat at my desk. I sometimes don’t understand the boss.","checklist":["Usei **advérbios**","Usei **take a break**","Usei **understand**"],"words":"6 linhas"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “accent” mean?","opts":["entender","sotaque","deveria"],"ans":1,"why":"**accent** = sotaque."},{"q":"What does “understand” mean?","opts":["pausa","chegar","entender"],"ans":2,"why":"**understand** = entender."},{"q":"What does “break” mean?","opts":["pausa","deveria","perguntar"],"ans":0,"why":"**break** = pausa."},{"q":"What does “should” mean?","opts":["chegar","deveria","atrasado"],"ans":1,"why":"**should** = deveria."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}